UnitMinter::constructor
├── when the token is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the voter is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the splitter is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the operator is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the initial base rate is zero
│   └── it should revert with InvalidBaseRate
├── when the initial base rate exceeds the maximum base rate
│   └── it should revert with BaseRateTooHigh
├── when the max base rate change cap is zero
│   └── it should revert with MaxBaseRateChangeCapTooLow
├── when the max base rate change cap exceeds the weekly maximum rate change
│   └── it should revert with MaxBaseRateChangeCapTooHigh
├── when the max base rate change exceeds its cap
│   └── it should revert with MaxBaseRateChangeTooHigh
├── when the min cooldown is zero
│   └── it should revert with MinCooldownTooLow
├── when the min cooldown exceeds the max cooldown
│   └── it should revert with InvalidCooldownRange
├── when the base rate update cooldown is below the minimum cooldown
│   └── it should revert with CooldownTooLow
├── when the base rate update cooldown exceeds the maximum cooldown
│   └── it should revert with CooldownTooHigh
├── when the rate controls exceed the discrete cooldown derived maximum
│   └── it should revert with RateControlsTooAggressive
├── when the max band floor cap is zero
│   └── it should revert with BandFloorCapTooLow
├── when the max band floor cap reaches the maximum pips
│   └── it should revert with BandFloorCapTooWide
├── when the max band ceiling cap is zero
│   └── it should revert with BandCeilingCapTooLow
├── when the max band ceiling exceeds the maximum pips
│   └── it should revert with BandCeilingCapTooWide
├── when the splitter is the minter address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSplitter
├── when the team rate exceeds the maximum team rate
│   └── it should revert with TeamRateTooHigh
├── when the initial next base rate update overflows
│   └── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast
├── when migration open is zero
│   └── it should revert with InvalidActivationTimestamp
├── when migration open is in the past
│   └── it should revert with InvalidActivationTimestamp
├── when migration open equals current timestamp
│   └── it should revert with InvalidActivationTimestamp
├── when migration open is not epoch aligned
│   └── it should revert with InvalidActivationTimestamp
└── when all inputs are valid
    ├── it should set the immutable dependencies
    ├── it should set ACTIVATION_TIMESTAMP to one week after migrationOpen
    ├── it should set the immutable configuration caps
    ├── it should leave dynamicRate at zero
    ├── it should set lastCapUpdate to ACTIVATION TIMESTAMP
    ├── it should set the mutable configuration
    ├── it should leave fed unset
    ├── it should leave the rate band unset
    └── it should leave the dynamic rate module unset

UnitMinter::MAX_BASE_RATE
└── it should expose the exact maximum base rate that keeps Voter arithmetic within uint256

UnitMinter::mint
├── when the caller is not the voter
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotVoter
├── when the amount is below the minimum mint amount
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the mint would exceed the emissions cap
│   └── it should revert with CapExceeded
├── when the recipient amount fits but the recipient and team total exceeds the emissions cap
│   ├── it should mint _amount to _recipient
│   ├── it should mint _splitterShare to SPLITTER
│   └── it should increase emissionsMinted by _amount
├── when the cumulative total exceeds the emissions cap and the amount alone fits
│   └── it should revert with CapExceeded
├── when a second mint follows an earlier mint
│   └── it should increase emissionsMinted by both amounts
└── given the accrual segment is live
    ├── when the team rate is zero
    │   ├── it should mint _amount to _recipient
    │   ├── it should not mint zero _splitterShare to SPLITTER
    │   ├── it should increase emissionsMinted by _amount
    │   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
    │   └── it should emit Minted with _recipient, _amount and zero _splitterShare
    ├── when the team rate is not zero
    │   ├── it should mint _amount to _recipient
    │   ├── it should mint _splitterShare to SPLITTER
    │   ├── it should increase emissionsMinted by _amount
    │   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
    │   └── it should emit Minted with _recipient, _amount and _splitterShare
    └── when the team rate is not zero and the splitter share has a remainder
        ├── it should mint _amount to _recipient
        ├── it should mint the rounded down _splitterShare to SPLITTER
        ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
        └── it should emit Minted with _recipient, _amount and the rounded down _splitterShare

UnitMinter::setOperator
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
├── when the operator is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with ZeroAddress
├── when the operator equals fed
│   └── it should revert with OperatorFEDCollision
└── when the operator is valid
    ├── it should update operator with _operator
    └── it should emit OperatorSet with _operator

UnitMinter::setFED
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
├── when fed equals operator
│   └── it should revert with OperatorFEDCollision
└── when fed is valid
    ├── it should update fed with _fed
    └── it should emit FEDSet with _fed

UnitMinter::setMaxBaseRateChangePips
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   ├── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the max base rate change pips exceeds the immutable cap
│   ├── it should revert with MaxBaseRateChangeTooHigh
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the max base rate change pips exceeds the discrete cooldown derived maximum
│   ├── it should revert with RateControlsTooAggressive
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the transition delay overflows
│   ├── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast
│   ├── it should leave maxBaseRateChangePips unchanged
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
└── when the max base rate change pips is valid
    ├── when the minimum transition deadline is later than next base rate update
    │   ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    ├── when the minimum transition deadline is not later than next base rate update
    │   ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    │   ├── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
    │   └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    ├── when using a six day cooldown at the discrete derived maximum
    │   ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    ├── when the cooldown divides the week at the discrete derived maximum
    │   ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    ├── when the value equals the current value
    │   ├── it should keep maxBaseRateChangePips unchanged
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips
    └── when next base rate update equals the transition delay
        ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with _maxBaseRateChangePips
        ├── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
        └── it should emit MaxBaseRateChangePipsSet with _maxBaseRateChangePips

UnitMinter::setBaseRateUpdateCooldown
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   ├── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the base rate update cooldown is below the minimum cooldown
│   ├── it should revert with CooldownTooLow
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the base rate update cooldown exceeds the maximum cooldown
│   ├── it should revert with CooldownTooHigh
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the current max base rate change exceeds the discrete cooldown derived maximum
│   ├── it should revert with RateControlsTooAggressive
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
├── when the transition delay overflows
│   ├── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast
│   ├── it should leave baseRateUpdateCooldown unchanged
│   └── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
└── when the base rate update cooldown is valid
    ├── when the minimum transition deadline is later than next base rate update
    │   ├── it should update baseRateUpdateCooldown with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit BaseRateUpdateCooldownSet with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
    ├── when the minimum transition deadline is not later than next base rate update
    │   ├── it should update baseRateUpdateCooldown with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
    │   ├── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
    │   └── it should emit BaseRateUpdateCooldownSet with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
    ├── when the value equals the current value
    │   ├── it should keep baseRateUpdateCooldown unchanged
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp plus one week
    │   └── it should emit BaseRateUpdateCooldownSet with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
    └── when next base rate update is after the transition delay
        ├── it should update baseRateUpdateCooldown with _baseRateUpdateCooldown
        ├── it should leave nextBaseRateUpdate unchanged
        └── it should emit BaseRateUpdateCooldownSet with _baseRateUpdateCooldown

UnitMinter::rateControlSetters
├── when both setters are called in the same block
│   ├── it should update baseRateUpdateCooldown with the new cooldown
│   ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with the new max
│   └── it should set nextBaseRateUpdate to block.timestamp plus one week exactly once
└── when changing from six day controls to seven day controls
    ├── it should update baseRateUpdateCooldown with the seven day cooldown
    ├── it should update maxBaseRateChangePips with the weekly maximum
    ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with the transition time plus one week
    ├── it should keep setBaseRate blocked at the stale six day deadline
    └── it should allow setBaseRate at the extended one week deadline

UnitMinter::setTeamRate
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
├── when the team rate exceeds the maximum team rate
│   └── it should revert with TeamRateTooHigh
└── when the team rate is valid
    ├── it should update teamRate with _teamRate
    └── it should emit TeamRateSet with _teamRate

UnitMinter::setRateBand
├── when the caller is not the governor
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotGovernor
├── when the floor pips exceeds the immutable cap
│   └── it should revert with BandFloorTooWide
├── when the ceiling pips exceeds the immutable cap
│   └── it should revert with BandCeilingTooWide
├── when the rate band is set before activation
│   ├── it should update bandFloorPips with _floorPips
│   ├── it should update bandCeilingPips with _ceilingPips
│   ├── it should emit RateBandSet with _floorPips and _ceilingPips
│   └── it should leave the emissions cap at zero
├── when the rate band is set after activation
│   ├── it should update bandFloorPips with _floorPips
│   ├── it should update bandCeilingPips with _ceilingPips
│   ├── it should emit RateBandSet with _floorPips and _ceilingPips
│   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
│   └── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp
└── when accruing at the maximum base rate and the widest band over the full timestamp horizon
    ├── it should expose twice the maximum base rate as the effective rate
    └── it should accrue the emissions cap without overflowing

UnitMinter::setBaseRate
├── when the caller is not the operator
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotOperator
├── when the new rate is zero
│   └── it should revert with InvalidBaseRate
├── when the new rate exceeds the maximum base rate
│   └── it should revert with BaseRateTooHigh
├── when the cooldown is active
│   └── it should revert with CooldownActive
├── when the new rate equals the current base rate
│   └── it should revert with SameRate
├── when the rate change above base exceeds the max change
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when using a concrete rate above the maximum change
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when using a concrete active max base rate change
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when the rate change below base exceeds the max change
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when using a concrete rate below the maximum change
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when the rate change equals the rounded up max change with a remainder
│   ├── it should update baseRate with _newRate
│   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp + baseRateUpdateCooldown
│   └── it should emit BaseRateSet with _newRate
├── when the rate change exceeds the rounded up max change with a remainder
│   └── it should revert with RateChangeExceedsMax
├── when the rate change bound is at the lowest possible values
│   └── it should allow a minimum rate change of one
├── when the next base rate update overflows
│   └── it should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast
├── when timestamp is before activation and rate change is valid
│   ├── it should update baseRate with _newRate
│   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp + baseRateUpdateCooldown
│   └── it should emit BaseRateSet with _newRate
└── given the accrual segment is live
    ├── when the rate change above base is valid
    │   ├── it should update baseRate with _newRate
    │   ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp + baseRateUpdateCooldown
    │   ├── it should emit BaseRateSet with _newRate
    │   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
    │   └── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp
    └── when the rate change below base is valid
        ├── it should update baseRate with _newRate
        ├── it should update nextBaseRateUpdate with block.timestamp + baseRateUpdateCooldown
        ├── it should emit BaseRateSet with _newRate
        ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
        └── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp

UnitMinter::setDynamicRateModule
├── when the caller is not fed
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotFED
├── when the caller is fed and the new module is nonzero
│   ├── it should update dynamicRateModule with _module
│   ├── it should preserve the current dynamic rate target
│   └── it should emit DynamicRateModuleSet with _module
├── when the caller is fed and the new module is zero and a dynamic target exists
│   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the outgoing effective rate
│   ├── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp
│   ├── it should clear the dynamic rate target
│   ├── it should return the base rate
│   ├── it should clear the dynamic rate module
│   ├── it should emit DynamicRateSet with zero
│   └── it should emit DynamicRateModuleSet with zero
└── when the caller is fed and the new module is zero and no dynamic target exists
    ├── it should not accrue the emissions cap
    ├── it should leave lastCapUpdate at ACTIVATION TIMESTAMP
    ├── it should not emit DynamicRateSet
    ├── it should clear the dynamic rate module
    └── it should emit DynamicRateModuleSet with zero

UnitMinter::setDynamicRate
├── when the caller is not the dynamic rate module
│   └── it should revert with CallerNotDynamicRateModule
└── given the caller is the dynamic rate module
    ├── when set before activation
    │   ├── it should store the rate
    │   ├── it should emit DynamicRateSet with the rate
    │   └── it should leave the emissions cap at zero
    ├── when set at exactly activation
    │   ├── it should store the rate
    │   ├── it should leave the emissions cap at zero
    │   └── it should leave lastCapUpdate at ACTIVATION TIMESTAMP
    └── given the accrual segment is live
        ├── when set after activation
        │   ├── it should store the rate
        │   ├── it should emit DynamicRateSet with the rate
        │   ├── it should accrue the emissions cap at the effective rate
        │   └── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp
        └── when a second push follows an earlier segment
            ├── it should accrue the sum of both segments at their own rates
            └── it should advance lastCapUpdate to the current timestamp

UnitMinter::emissionRate
├── when the timestamp is before activation
│   └── it should return zero
├── when the timestamp equals activation
│   └── it should return the base rate
├── when the dynamic rate is zero and the rate band is set
│   └── it should return the base rate
├── when the rate band is unset
│   └── it should return the base rate
├── when the dynamic rate is below the floor
│   └── it should return the floor rate
├── when the dynamic rate is above the ceiling
│   └── it should return the ceiling rate
├── when widening the ceiling band with an unchanged target
│   ├── it should return the narrow ceiling rate before the widening
│   └── it should return the wider ceiling rate after the widening
├── when the dynamic rate is below the base and above the floor
│   └── it should return the dynamic rate
├── when the dynamic rate is above the base and below the ceiling
│   └── it should return the dynamic rate
├── when using a concrete rate below the floor
│   └── it should return the floor rate
├── when the dynamic rate is below the base and the floor width rounds down to zero
│   └── it should return the base rate
├── when the dynamic rate is above the base and the ceiling width rounds down to zero
│   └── it should return the base rate
├── when the dynamic rate is below the floor and the floor width has a remainder
│   └── it should return the floor rate
├── when using a concrete rate below the base and above the floor
│   └── it should return the dynamic rate
├── when using a concrete rate above the base and below the ceiling
│   └── it should return the dynamic rate
├── when using a concrete rate above the ceiling
│   └── it should return the ceiling rate
└── when the dynamic rate is above the ceiling and the ceiling width has a remainder
    └── it should return the ceiling rate
